@startuml
actor Recipient
participant ActivationPage as SPA
participant ActivationApi as Client
participant ActivationController as API
participant ActivationService as App
participant IActivationRepository as Repo
participant "IPasswordHasher\n(BcryptPasswordHasher adapter)" as Hasher
Recipient -> SPA : Open invitation link
note right of SPA : Read activationToken and clear the query parameter.
SPA -> Client : inspect(token)
Client -> API : POST /activation/inspect
API -> App : inspect(token)
App -> Repo : findEligibleBinding(SHA-256(token), now)
break Unavailable invitation
 App --> API : Invitation unavailable
 API --> Client : 400
 Client --> SPA : Show recovery guidance
end
App --> API : InvitationMethodDTO(method)
API --> Client : 200 method
Client --> SPA : InvitationMethodDTO
alt Method is EXTERNAL
 ref over SPA, App : SD 2 — startExternal(token)
else Method is LOCAL
loop Initial token-only submission and retry if password setup is required
 SPA -> Client : local(token, password?)
 Client -> API : POST /activation/local
 alt Malformed input
  API --> Client : 400 validation error
 else Valid request shape
  API -> App : activateLocal(token, password?)
  App -> Repo : findBinding(SHA-256(token))
  alt Unknown token
   App --> API : Invitation unavailable
  else Supplied password fails local policy
   App --> API : 400 validation error
  else Binding and input eligible
   opt First password supplied
    App -> Hasher : hash(password)
    Hasher --> App : passwordHash
   end
   note right of App
    Build the domain ActivationCredential.local(...):
    Password.createFromHash(passwordHash) when supplied,
    or no password when confirming with the token alone.
   end note
   ref over App, Repo : SD 3 — commitActivation(binding, credential)
  end
  API --> Client : 200 nextSignIn or error
 end
 Client --> SPA : ActivationResult or mapped error
 alt Valid invitation requires first password
  SPA --> Recipient : Show password setup form
  Recipient -> SPA : Set password and submit
 else Success or other error
  SPA --> Recipient : Show confirmation and local sign-in, or recovery guidance
 end
end
end
@enduml
